IMPORT prelude

-- ccc13-logic.l4 -- three-valued helpers over MAYBE BOOLEAN, written by part agent ccc13.
-- They carry the prefix `ccc13` and not a section label, because they implement no provision: they combine answers.
-- Every part that joins MAYBE BOOLEAN answers needs the same three; they are listed in NEEDS-CORE.md for the lead to hoist.
-- JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no, NOTHING is "not covered". Kleene's rules, so a NOTHING is never turned into a FALSE:
--   all of:  any JUST FALSE gives JUST FALSE; otherwise any NOTHING gives NOTHING; otherwise JUST TRUE (an empty list gives JUST TRUE).
--   any of:  any JUST TRUE gives JUST TRUE; otherwise any NOTHING gives NOTHING; otherwise JUST FALSE (an empty list gives JUST FALSE).
--   not:     swaps JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE and leaves NOTHING alone.
-- The JUST FALSE and NOTHING results here are logic, not a decision of the text, so they carry no FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.

GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc13 all of` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS NOTHING) answers
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc13 any of` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) answers
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS NOTHING) answers
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc13 not` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
